# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default. A shell script with CRLF fails
# the instant it runs on Linux, because the shebang is read as `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`
# and there is no binary called "bash\r" — the container exits immediately with
#
#   env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree on every platform avoids that entirely.

* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the exception: batch files genuinely need CRLF, and misparse labels
# and multi-line blocks without it.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never rewrite binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gz  binary
*.xz  binary
*.zip binary
*.fits binary
*.npz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
